
## Bandit Level 15 → Level 16

**Challenge:** 

The password for the next level can be retrieved by submitting the password of the current level to port 30001 on localhost using SSL/TLS encryption.

Helpful note: Getting “DONE”, “RENEGOTIATING” or “KEYUPDATE”? Read the “CONNECTED COMMANDS” section in the manpage.

Commands you may need to solve this level
ssh, telnet, nc, ncat, socat, openssl, s_client, nmap, netstat, ss


**Solution & Explanation:****
```
STEP 1: cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit15
# read the current password (bandit15)
# this is what the SSL service expects as input

STEP 2: openssl s_client -connect localhost:30001
# openssl s_client opens an SSL/TLS-encrypted connection
# port 30001 specifically requires SSL (plain nc will NOT work)

STEP 3: paste the bandit15 password and press Enter
# the server verifies the password
# if correct, it sends back the bandit16 password

```
